Track 2: "Can You Hear the Tape Head Rusting?"
- Story & Context: Huddled beside an illegal kerosene burner inside the Vatnajökull ice hollow, synth programmer Sean "Casket" Vance broke down on open intercom, confessing he had intentionally exposed his beloved synthesizers to the cave's perpetual condensation until their circuit boards oxidized into turquoise mold. The temperature rose just enough to send oily black meltwater trickling down his wool sleeves, causing a weeping CS-80 brass patch to slip out of tune into a seasick, devastating lament while monstrous Big Beat drums pounded against the hollow ice walls. Unable to process the sudden passing of his brother, Vance locked the chamber's safety gate and slammed his faders upward, weaponizing the ceiling’s rhythmic drips as high-frequency percussion against his own regret. Over the swampy 303 acid line, he screamed into a corroded CB radio: "Tell me which memory is heavy enough to anchor us."
